29", "kind": "thrust_cap"}, {"date": "2026-07-30", "kind": "turned_fading"}], "study": {"state": "Every thrust in the study came out of a washout, but washouts often lasted weeks before one came (industries spent 13% of all days in Washout). On its own a washout says nothing about timing.", "market": "Market context mattered more than the thrust type. Thrusts while the Nifty 50 was below its 200-day average were followed by +6.5 points over 60 sessions even without 2020 (62% rose 15% first; 215 cases in 36 weeks); thrusts while it was above, by -2.2 points. This split was examined after seeing the results, and 36 separate weeks is a small sample.", "rallies": "Of 285 big rallies (an industry index rising 25% or more within 120 sessions of a 60-session low), a C or CAP thrust came within 20 sessions of the low in 145 (51%), typically 5 sessions after it.", "leader_flag": "Full flags (industry 15% or more below its high): in 644 cases the stock did 6.0% better than its industry over the next 120 sessions on average (median +2.8%; 55% beat it), while an average stock of the same industry on the same days did -0.2% (43% beat it). In 2020 flagged stocks did 3.9% worse. The softer 10-15% tier showed no difference (+0.8% average, median -1.5%; 837 cases).", "quarter": "At a C thrust, the top quarter by 6-month return did 0.8 points better than its industry over the next 60 sessions and the bottom quarter 1.6 points worse; the median stock in every quarter trailed the equal-weighted industry index. After a CAP thrust there was no clear order.", "bottom": "No meaningful difference: at thrusts, stocks that bottomed before their industry and were above their 20-day average did 0.2 points better than their industry over 60 sessions; the others 0.3-0.6 points worse.", "limits": "NSE daily data from Jan 2016; cases from Jan 2017 to Oct 2026 across 46 NSE industry and sector groups. The stock list is rebuilt every month from what was known then, including companies later delisted.